\section{The \texttt{streams} subcommand}

The [[streams]] subcommand lists all streams (channels) on the server.
This is useful for discovering where to send messages---particularly
on a server with many streams where the web interface's sidebar
becomes unwieldy.

<<functions>>=
def _streams_handler(
    ctx: typer.Context,
    patterns: Annotated[
        Optional[list[str]],
        typer.Argument(
            help="filter streams by name (regex; repeat to OR several)",
        ),
    ] = None,
    unread: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--unread",
            "-U",
            help="only show streams with unread messages",
        ),
    ] = False,
):
    """List available streams."""
    streams_command(
        _get_client_from_context(ctx),
        SimpleNamespace(patterns=patterns, unread=unread),
    )
@

Like the user-targeting commands, [[streams]] accepts zero or more regex
patterns and ORs them together.
We still sort the output alphabetically for readability.
The unread view uses the unread summary helper above and sums per-topic
counts back into per-stream counts, because Zulip reports unread channel
state one topic at a time.

<<functions>>=
def streams_command(client, args):
    """List available streams."""
    result = _require_success(client.get_streams())

    pattern_strs = getattr(
        args,
        "patterns",
        getattr(args, "pattern", None),
    )
    patterns = _compile_patterns(pattern_strs)

    if args.unread:
        unread_topics, old_unreads_missing = (
            _get_unread_topics_by_stream(client)
        )
        rows = []
        for stream in sorted(result["streams"],
                             key=lambda s: s["name"]):
            if not _matches_patterns([stream["name"]], patterns):
                continue
            topics = unread_topics.get(stream["stream_id"])
            if not topics:
                continue
            rows.append((
                stream["name"],
                _format_unread_count(
                    sum(topics.values()),
                    old_unreads_missing,
                ),
            ))
        _print_unread_rows("Stream", rows)
        return

    for stream in sorted(result["streams"],
                         key=lambda s: s["name"]):
        if not _matches_patterns([stream["name"]], patterns):
            continue
        print(stream["name"])
@

