\section{The \texttt{dm} subcommand}

The [[dm]] command mirrors [[read]], but for direct messages instead of
stream history.
With no positional arguments it reads every direct message visible in the
current user's personal history; with one or more [[USER]] regexes it
resolves those users and narrows to the exact 1:1 or group conversation
with that set of participants.

Zulip's search model makes the conversation case especially clean:
[[dm]] accepts a list of user IDs, and the server treats that list as an
order-insensitive conversation identity.
That means repeated or overlapping regexes can be silently deduplicated
before we build the narrow, with no ambiguity about which conversation we
mean.

<<functions>>=
def _dm_handler(
    ctx: typer.Context,
    users: Annotated[
        Optional[list[str]],
        typer.Argument(
            help="direct-message participant regex; repeat to OR "
                 "several patterns over full name, Zulip email, "
                 "and delivery email",
            autocompletion=complete_user_emails,
        ),
    ] = None,
    unread: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--unread",
            "-U",
            help="only show unread messages",
        ),
    ] = False,
    mark_as_read: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--mark-as-read/--no-mark-as-read",
            help="mark printed messages as read",
        ),
    ] = False,
):
    """Read direct messages."""
    dm_command(
        _get_client_from_context(ctx),
        SimpleNamespace(
            users=users,
            unread=unread,
            mark_as_read=mark_as_read,
        ),
    )
@

The direct-message reader reuses the same member resolver as [[send]], so
regexes over full names, Zulip emails, and delivery emails behave the
same everywhere.
Bots stay eligible participants, deactivated accounts do not, and a
conversation narrow is only built after repeated matches have collapsed
to one stable-sorted user-ID list.

<<functions>>=
def _dm_narrow_for_users(client, user_patterns):
    """Return a Zulip narrow for all DMs or one DM conversation."""
    if not user_patterns:
        return [{"operator": "is", "operand": "dm"}]

    users = _resolve_direct_recipients(client, user_patterns)
    if not users:
        _exit_with_error(
            f"dm {_describe_patterns(user_patterns)} matched "
            "no active users"
        )

    return [{
        "operator": "dm",
        "operand": [user["user_id"] for user in users],
    }]
@

<<functions>>=
def dm_command(client, args):
    """Read direct messages, optionally for one conversation."""
    narrow = _dm_narrow_for_users(client, args.users)
    if args.unread:
        narrow.append({"operator": "is", "operand": "unread"})
    _read_messages(client, narrow, mark_as_read=args.mark_as_read)
