\subsection{Indexing without endangering the read}

Indexing is a side effect of reading, and a side effect must never be
able to break the thing it rides along with.
A read-only data directory, a corrupted database, a filesystem whose
locking SQLite cannot use---none of those are the user's problem when
they asked to read a topic, so every failure here is swallowed.

The opt-out is an environment variable rather than a flag.
A flag would have to be threaded identically through [[read]], [[dm]],
[[search]], and [[bot]], and nobody wants to decide this once per
invocation; the realistic preference is \enquote{on this machine,
never}, which is exactly what an environment variable expresses.

<<constants>>=
TERM_INDEX_DISABLED_ENV = "ZULIPCLI_NO_TERM_INDEX"
<<functions>>=
def _index_messages_safely(client, messages):
    """Index `messages`, never failing the caller's read."""
    if not messages or os.environ.get(TERM_INDEX_DISABLED_ENV):
        return
    try:
        _index_messages(client, messages)
    except Exception:
        pass
@

<<test functions>>=
